      {
        "name": "EnvRegistration",
        "kind": "class",
        "module": "cuprum.context.registration",
        "path": "cuprum/context/registration.py",
        "line": 228,
        "display": "class EnvRegistration(overlay: cabc.Mapping[str, str]) -> None",
        "doc": {
          "summary": "Registration handle for a scoped environment overlay.",
          "body": [
            "The overlay is layered on top of any overlay already present in the current context; nested registrations therefore behave as a stack. The token-restoration discipline is documented on <code>_TokenRegistration</code>.",
            "The overlay itself is overlay-only. The live <code>os.environ</code> is read at subprocess spawn time (see <a href=\"#resolve_env\"><code>resolve_env</code></a>), so any updates to the process environment after the registration is created — for example via <code>pytest</code>'s <code>monkeypatch.setenv</code> — remain visible to subprocesses spawned inside the scope. This is the behaviour the issue requires."
          ]
        },
