      {
        "name": "resolve_env",
        "kind": "function",
        "module": "cuprum.context.env_overlay",
        "path": "cuprum/context/env_overlay.py",
        "line": 73,
        "display": "def resolve_env(\n    *layers: cabc.Mapping[str, str] | None,\n) -> dict[str, str] | None",
        "doc": {
          "summary": "Merge <code>os.environ</code> (read live) with the supplied overlay layers.",
          "body": [
            "Layers are applied left-to-right; later values win. <code>None</code> *and empty* layers are skipped — an empty overlay contributes nothing, so treating it as a no-op avoids an unnecessary copy of <code>os.environ</code> and lets the subprocess inherit the parent environment directly. When every layer is skipped the function returns <code>None</code> so callers may pass it through to <code>subprocess</code> APIs to mean *inherit the parent environment unchanged*.",
            "The call to <code>os.environ.copy</code> is deferred until at least one overlay is non-empty, so the result reflects whatever the process environment looks like at the moment of resolution — the exact behaviour the issue requires."
          ],
          "sections": [
            {
              "title": "Parameters",
              "fields": [
                {
                  "name": "*layers",
                  "type": "collections.abc.Mapping[str, str] | None",
                  "description": "Overlay layers applied left-to-right over a live copy of <code>os.environ</code>; later values win. <code>None</code> and empty layers are skipped."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "title": "Returns",
              "fields": [
                {
                  "name": "",
                  "type": "dict[str, str] | None",
                  "description": "The merged environment mapping, or <code>None</code> when every layer is <code>None</code> or empty (meaning *inherit the parent environment unchanged*)."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
