        "display": "class RelayFallback(\n    stream: EchoStream,\n    error_category: EchoErrorCategory,\n)",
        "doc": {
          "summary": "One handled echo-disablement recorded on a command's result.",
          "body": [
            "A text-only echo sink rejected the subprocess output, so the echo for that stream's drain was disabled while the stream itself kept being consumed and, when enabled, captured. One record describes one handled disablement for one stream: later chunks and the final decoder flush never re-enter the failed write, so a drain contributes at most one record."
          ],
          "examples": "A stdout echo that could not encode its payload::\n\n    fallback = RelayFallback(\n        stream=EchoStream.STDOUT,\n        error_category=EchoErrorCategory.UNICODE_ENCODE,\n    )\n    assert fallback.stream == \"stdout\""
        },
